hadiths[26]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27425","Abd al-Razzaq said: Mamar narrated to us from Ibn Tawus from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab from Umm Hani, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted on the day of the Conquest at the upper part of Makkah, and I came to him, and Abu Dharr came with a large bowl containing water. She said: I could see in it the trace of dough. She said: So he - meaning Abu Dharr - screened him, and he washed, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed eight rakahs, and that was in the forenoon."
"27426","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ata informed me from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: I entered to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest while he was in a tent of his, and I found he had washed with water that was in a bowl; I could see in it the trace of dough, and I found him praying Duha. I said: I think this report of Umm Hani is established. He said: Yes. Ibn Bakr said: al-Duha."
"27427","Abd al-Razzaq said: Mamar informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Umm Hani - and he was staying with her - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest was screened, and he washed in the forenoon, then prayed eight rakahs; it is not known whether his standing was longer or his prostration."
"27428","Sufyan from Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid from Umm Hani, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Makkah once, and he had four braids."
"27429","Hammad ibn Usamah said: Hatim ibn Abi Sagheerah informed me, and Rawh said: Hatim ibn Abi Sagheerah narrated to us, he said: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us from Abu Salih, the freedman of Umm Hani - Rawh said in his hadith: Umm Hani narrated to me - and she said to me: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about His saying, Exalted: And you commit evil in your assembly. He said: They used to throw pebbles at travelers and mock them; so that is the evil they used to commit. Rawh said: So that is His saying, Exalted: And you commit evil in your assembly."
"27430","Zayd ibn al-Hubab from Ibn Abi Dhib from al-Maqburi from Abu Murrah, the freedman of Aqil ibn Abi Talib, from Fakhitah Umm Hani, she said: When it was the day of the conquest of Makkah, I gave protection to two relatives by marriage of mine from the polytheists, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appeared, with the dust of the road upon him, in a sheet wrapped in it. When he saw me, he said: Welcome to Fakhitah Umm Hani. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given protection to two relatives by marriage of mine from the polytheists. So he said: We have given protection to whom you gave protection, and we have granted safety to whom you granted safety. Then he ordered Fatimah, and she poured water for him, and he washed with it, then prayed eight rakahs in the garment, wrapped in it, and that was on the day of the conquest of Makkah in the forenoon."
"27431","Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi said: Shubah narrated to us from Jadah from Umm Hani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her and called for a drink, and he drank, then handed it to her, and she drank, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, I was fasting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The voluntary faster is master of himself; if he wishes, he fasts, and if he wishes, he breaks his fast. He said: I said to him: Did you hear it yourself from Umm Hani? He said: No; Abu Salih and our family narrated it to me from Umm Hani."
"27432","Sulayman said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I used to hear Simak saying: Ibn Umm Hani narrated to us, so I came to the better of them and the more excellent, and asked him, and he was called Jadah."
"27433","Abd al-Samad said: Thabit ibn Yazid Abu Zayd narrated to us: Hilal - meaning Ibn Khabbab - narrated to us, he said: I and Mujahid stayed with Yahya ibn Jadah ibn Umm Hani, and he narrated to us from Umm Hani, she said: I hear the recitation of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the middle of the night while I am on this rooftop of mine, and he is at the Kabah."
"27434","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr and Ibn Abi Bukayr said: Ibrahim ibn Nafi narrated to us from Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid from Umm Hani, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Maymunah washed from one vessel, a large bowl in which there was the trace of dough."
"27435","Yazid ibn Harun said: Muhammad - meaning Ibn Amr - informed us from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn from Abu Murrah, the freedman of Umm Hani - Muhammad said: And I saw Abu Murrah, and he was an old man who had met Umm Hani - from Umm Hani, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the Conquest, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given protection to two relatives by marriage of mine, and the son of my mother claims he will kill them - meaning Ali. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have given protection to whom you gave protection, O Umm Hani. And water was poured for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he washed, then wrapped himself in a garment over him and crossed its ends over his shoulder, then prayed Duha, eight rakahs."
"27436","Aswad ibn Amir said: Israil narrated to us from Simak from a man from Umm Hani, she said: When it was the day of the conquest of Makkah, Fatimah came and sat on his left, and Umm Hani came and sat on his right, and the slave girl came with a drink, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it and drank, then handed it to Umm Hani on his right, and she said: I was fasting. So he said to her: Is it something you are making up that is due upon you? She said: No. He said: It will not harm you then."
"27437","Yala ibn Ubayd said: Ismail - meaning Ibn Abi Khalid - narrated to us from Abu Salih from Umm Hani, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered on the day of the conquest of Makkah, they screened him, and he was brought water and washed, then prayed Duha, eight rakahs, which no one saw him pray after it."
"27438","Harun said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us from Ibn Shihab, he said: Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to me that his father Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal narrated to him that Umm Hani bint Abi Talib informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came after the day had risen on the day of the Conquest, and he ordered a garment and was screened with it, then washed, then stood and bowed eight rakahs; I do not know whether his standing in them was longer or his bowing or his prostration; all of that from him was close. She said: I never saw him pray it before nor after."
"27439","Muhammad ibn Jafar said: Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah from Ibn Abi Layla, he said: No one informed me that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying Duha except Umm Hani, for she narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered her house on the day of the conquest of Makkah and washed and prayed eight rakahs; she never saw him pray any prayer lighter than it, except that he completed the bowing and prostration."
"27440","Muhammad ibn Jafar said: Shubah narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn al-Harith about the Duha prayer, so he said: I met the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while they were numerous, and none of them narrated to me that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying Duha except Umm Hani, for she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me on the day of the Conquest, a Friday, and washed, then prayed eight rakahs."
"27441","Ibrahim ibn Khalid said: Rabah narrated to me from Mamar from Abu Uthman al-Jahshi from Musa - or: so-and-so ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rabiah - from Umm Hani: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Take sheep, O Umm Hani, for they go out in the evening with good and come in the morning with good."
"27442","Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi said: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to me from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn from Abu Murrah from Umm Hani, that she saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in one garment, crossing its ends, eight rakahs at Makkah on the day of the Conquest."
"27443","Waki said: Shubah narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: No one informed us that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Duha except Umm Hani, for she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered my house and washed on the day of the conquest of Makkah, then prayed eight rakahs, lightening the bowing and prostration in them."
"27444","Waki said: Misar narrated to us from Abu al-Ala al-Abdi from Yahya ibn Jadah from Umm Hani, she said: I used to hear the recitation of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night while I was on my rooftop."
"27445","Waki said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi from Abu Murrah, the freedman of Fakhitah Umm Hani, from Fakhitah Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: When it was the day of the conquest of Makkah, I gave protection to two men from my relatives by marriage, and I put them in a house and locked the door upon them, and the son of my mother, Ali ibn Abi Talib, came and attacked them with the sword. She said: So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not find him, and I found Fatimah, and she was harsher to me than her husband. She said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, with the trace of dust upon him, and I told him, so he said: O Umm Hani, we have given protection to whom you gave protection, and we have granted safety to whom you granted safety."
"27446","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi from Malik from Abu al-Nadr from Abu Murrah, the freedman of Aqil ibn Abi Talib, from Umm Hani, that she went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest. She said: So I found him washing, and Fatimah was screening him with a garment, and I greeted, and that was in the forenoon. So he said: Who is this? So I said: I am Umm Hani. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the son of my mother claims he will kill a man I gave protection to, so-and-so ibn Hubayrah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have given protection to whom you gave protection, O Umm Hani. And when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his washing, he stood and prayed eight rakahs, wrapped in a garment."
"27447","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi this hadith: Malik from Abu al-Nadr, the freedman of Umayr ibn Ubaydullah, that Abu Murrah, the freedman of Umm Hani, informed him that he heard Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, who went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest, then he mentioned the hadith."
"27448","Muhammad ibn Jafar said: Shubah narrated to us from Jadah from Umm Hani - and she is his grandmother - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her on the day of the Conquest, and he was brought a drink and drank, then handed it to me, so I said: I am fasting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The voluntary faster is master over himself; if you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break your fast."
"27449","Bahz said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us from Harun, son of the daughter of Umm Hani - or: son of Umm Hani - from Umm Hani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank a drink and handed it to her to drink, so she said: I am fasting, but I disliked to return your leftover. So he said - meaning: If it is making up from Ramadan, then make up a day in its place, and if it is voluntary, then if you wish, make it up, and if you wish, do not make it up."
"27450","Abdullah said: I found in the book of my father: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us from Abu Salih from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, he said: She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me one day, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have grown old and weak - or as she said - so command me with a deed I can do while I am sitting. He said: Glorify Allah one hundred tasbihs, for they equal for you one hundred necks you free from the children of Ismail; and praise Allah one hundred praises, they equal for you one hundred horses, saddled and bridled, you carry upon them in the path of Allah; and magnify Allah one hundred takbirs, for they equal for you one hundred sacrificial camels, collared and accepted; and declare Allah one - one hundred tahlils. Ibn Khalaf said: I think he said: They fill what is between heaven and earth, and no deed is raised that day for anyone except one who comes with the like of what you brought."
